.TH CArrayDisplay n 03/08/98 "CADC"
.\".BS
.SH NAME
CArrayDisplay 
\- Create and manipulate a widget which displays a status record array. A record array is a set of records which have an index.
   e.g. resource0:name, resource1:name, ... resourcen:name
        resource0:type, resource1:type, ... resourcen:type
.sp
A set of records are all those with the same index numbers. In the example above resource0:name and resource0:type would be a record set.

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBCArrayDisplay\fI \fIpathName \fR?\fIoptions\fR?

.SH "INHERITANCE"
itk::Toplevel \<- iwidgets::Shell \<- iwidgets::Dialogshell \<- CArrayDisplay

.SO
\-background	\-cursor	\-foreground
\-selectbackground
.SE

.SH "ASSOCIATED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-cellbd\fR	\fB\-columnwidths\fR	\fB\-elementborderwidth\fR
\fB\-headings\fR	\fB\-hscrollmode\fR	\fB\-jump\fR
\fB\-labelbitmap\fR	\fB\-labelfont\fR	\fB\-labelimage\fR
\fB\-labelmargin\fR	\fB\-labelpos\fR	\fB\-labeltext\fR
\fB\-labelvariable\fR	\fB\-sbwidth\fR	\fB\-scrollmargin\fR
\fB\-troughcolor\fR	\fB\-vscrollmode\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBCTable\fR class manual entry for descriptions for the
above options.  These options are applied only to the table that is
displayed in the array window.

.SH "INHERITED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-clientdata\fR	\fB\-title\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBitk::Toplevel\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-master\fR	\fB\-modality\fR	\fB\-padx\fR
\fB\-pady\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBitk::Shell\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-buttonboxpadx\fR	\fB\-buttonboxpady\fR	\fB\-separator\fR
\fB\-thickness\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBitk::Dialogshell\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"

.OP \-arraysize arraySize Size
Specifies the number of records of each type that are in the status 
record array or the name of the status record whose value is the 
number of records.  For example, if we has the array records, 
.nf
.sp
    resource0:name, resource0:type, resource1:name, 
    resource1:type, resource3:name, and resource3:type.  
.fi
the array size would be 3. 

.OP \-inuse inUse InUse
Specifies the status record which indicates if a particular set of records
are being used. The status record specified should have a "%d" in it, this
part of the string is replaced with a numerical index.
If this record has "true" value then the record is
displayed.  An example of an in use status record is: resource%d:inUse, 
where "%d" is replaced by the appropriate index. If "resource0:inuse" is
"1" then the values for "resource0:name, resource0:type, ..." would be
displayed in the window.

.OP \-recordname recordNames RecordName
Specifies the list of status records that are to be displayed/monitored.
All of the records given should have the substring "%d" in them, this
substring will be replaced by a numerical index.
An example of this list is:
.nf
.sp
   {resource%d:name resource%d:type resource%d:used}
.fi

.OP \-rowcmd rowCmd Command
Specifies the command that is called when a row is added or changes 
position in the table. The table
window path name, the row of the table the record set is displayed in, 
and the numerical index of the record set will be appended to the
command.

.OP \-sortcmd sortCmd Command
Specifies the command to execute that provides the sorting
order of the status records being monitored. The default order is to 
sort by record index value, where the status record with the lowest 
index appears at the top of the window.  It is assumed that the specified
command return a list whose entries are the numerical indices of the
records being monitored.

.OP \-tablefont tableFont Font 
Specifies the font to use when drawing text inside the 
table portion. 

.OP \-tableheight tableheight Height
Specifies the height of the table portion.

.OP \-tablerelief tableRelief Relief
Specifies the 3-D border style around the table.

.OP \-tablewidth tableWidth Width
Specifies the width of the table portion.

.\".BE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBCArrayDisplay\fR command creates a new window (given by the
\fIpathName\fR argument) and makes it into a \fBCArrayDisplay\fR widget.
Additional options, described above, may be specified on the 
command line or in the option database to configure aspects of
the record array widget. The \fBCArrayDisplay\fR command returns its
\fIpathName\fR argument.  At the time this command is invoked,
there must not exist a window named \fIpathName\fR, but
\fIpathName\fR's parent must exist.

.SH "INHERITED COMMANDS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBactivate\fR	\fBadd\fR	\fBbuttonconfigure\fR
\fBcenter\fR	\fBdeactivate\fR	\fBdefault\fR
\fBdelete\fR	\fBhide\fR	\fBindex\fR
\fBinsert\fR	\fBinvoke\fR	\fBshow\fR
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBiwdigets::Dialogshell\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited commands


.SH "WIDGET COMMAND"
The \fBCArrayDisplay\fR command creates a new Tcl command whose
name is \fIpathName\fR.  This
command may be used to invoke various
operations on the widget.  It has the following general form:
.CS
\fIpathName method \fR?\fIarg arg ...\fR?
.CE
\fImethod\fR and the \fIarg\fRs
determine the exact behavior of the command.  
.PP
The following methods are possible for CArrayDisplay widgets:

.TP
\fIpathName \fBactivate\fR
If there are no records currently displayed a pop-up window is displayed
stating such.  Otherwise, the sets of records are displayed in the
status record array window. The window
waits based on the modality. For application and system modal  
activations, perform a grab operation, and wait for the result.   
The result may be returned via an argument to the deactivate
method.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcget\fR \fIoption\fR
Returns the current value of the configuration option given
by \fIoption\fR.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCArrayDisplay\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBchildsite\fR
Return the path name of the child site.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcomponent\fR ?\fIname\fR? ?\fIcommand arg arg ...\fR?
Used to query or access component widgets within the status array record
widget.  With no arguments, this returns a list of
symbolic names for component widgets that are accessible in the
current scope.  
.sp
If a symbolic \fIname\fR is specified this method returns the window
path name for that component.
.sp
Otherwise, the \fIcommand\fR and any remaining \fIarg\fR arguments
are invoked as a method on the component with the symbolic \fIname\fR.
This provides a well-defined mechanism for accessing internal components
without relying on specific window path names.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBconfig\fR
See \fBconfigure\fI.

.TP
\fIpathName\fR \fBconfigure\fR ?\fIoption\fR? ?\fIvalue option value ...\fR?
Query or modify the configuration options of the widget.
If no \fIoption\fR is specified, returns a list describing all of
the available options for \fIpathName\fR (see \fBTk_ConfigureInfo\fR for
information on the format of this list).  If \fIoption\fR is specified
with no \fIvalue\fR, then the command returns a list describing the
one named option (this list will be identical to the corresponding
sublist of the value returned if no \fIoption\fR is specified).  If
one or more \fIoption\-value\fR pairs are specified, then the command
modifies the given widget option(s) to have the given value(s);  in
this case the command returns an empty string.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCArrayDisplay\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBisa\fR \fBclassName\fR
Sets the status record array widget's class to the specified class name.

.SH "COMPONENTS"
.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBtable\fR
Class:  \fBCTable\fR
.fi
.IP
Table area where the status records are displayed.  The table is
not editable.  See the \fBCTable\fR widget for more information.

.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
.PP
No bindings are defined for this widget except those defined for the
various components this widget is comprised of.
.PP
See the \fBCTable\fR, \fBscrolledframe\fR, and \fBbutton\fR manual
entries for more information.

.SH EXAMPLE
.DS
 CDhgStatus dhsStatus "STO"
 set recordList [ list stoAction%dAction  stoAction%dReqId         \\
         stoAction%dOption stoAction%dActive  stoAction%dPosition ]
 set headings { Action "Request Id" Options } 
 CArrayDisplay .actionInfo dhsStatus -arraysize 5                  \\
        -cellbd 4                                                  \\
        -columnwidths { 10 10 20 }                                 \\
        -headings $headings                                        \\
        -hscrollmode dynamic                                       \\
        -inuse "stoAction%dInUse"                                  \\
        -labelmargin 30                                            \\
        -labeltext "Contents of the Action Queue"                  \\
        -recordnames $recordList                                   \\
        -tableheight 300                                           \\
        -tablewidth 400                                            \\
        -title "Actions"                                           \\
        -vscrollmode dynamic

 .actionInfo add Ok -command ".actionInfo deactivate" -text "Ok"
 .actionInfo activate
.DE

.SH AUTHOR
Shannon Jaeger

.SH KEYWORDS
status record, status record array, table, widget, 
